{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$f$ is a rational function.\n\nTo find the derivative of rational functions, we use **the quotient rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}\\right]\u0026=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)-u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{u'(x)v(x)-u(x)v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's differentiate!\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}f'(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{x^2-2}{x-1}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(x-1)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^2-2)-(x^2-2)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x-1)}{(x-1)^2}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{The quotient rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(x-1)(2x)-(x^2-2)(1)}{(x-1)^2}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }(x^2-2)\\text{ \u0026 }(x-1)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{2x^2-2x-x^2+2}{(x-1)^2}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Expand}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{x^2-2x+2}{(x-1)^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $f'(x)=\\dfrac{x^2-2x+2}{(x-1)^2}$, or any other equivalent form.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $f(x)=\\dfrac{x^2-2}{x-1}$.\n\n$f'(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":"0","simplify":false,"value":"\\frac{x^{2}-2x+2}{\\left(x-1\\right)^{2}}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"static":false,"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
